6) what is the difference between Additive, Semi-Additive and Non-additive facts?
==================================================================================

An additive fact is a measure in a fact table that can be fully summed across any of the dimensions associated with it.

show me sales amount per day
show me sales amount per customers
show me sales amount per store

so here sales amount is measure that can be aggregated across any of the dimensions like time, customer,store.

A semi-additive fact is a measure in a fact table that can be summed across few dimensions associated with it, but not all.

daily average balance of a bank account. this number can be summed up across customer dim but not with time dimension

because lets say my dialy average balance as of yday is 50$ and my daily avg balance for today is 60$ so if I want to do

a summation of it over the time it would mean 50 + 60 = 110 which is not right as we want the average.

A non-additive fact is a measure in a fact table that cannot be summed across any dimensions associated with it.

pre-calculated discount amount.

